-- title:
--   Generator and idempotent tower on the Eisenstein inertia Tate module
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with $2$ a non-unit of $B$ (the predicate [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16) for $q=2$). Write $J =$ `JZero p`, the degree-zero divisor class group of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, with its Hecke-algebra structure `heckeModuleBar p` over $\mathbb T =$ `HeckeAlg` $= \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,\mathbb{P}\,\mathbb Z$, and let $\Lambda \subseteq (\mathbb N \to J)$ be the intersection of [`TateModule 2 J`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) — the sequences $x$ with $2^n x_n = 0$ and $2x_{n+1} = x_n$ for all $n$ — with the subgroup of sequences all of whose components lie in the subgroup of $J$ generated by the displacements $\sigma\cdot x - x$, where $\sigma$ runs over the inertia subgroup of $B$ over $\mathbb Q$ (the image in $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of `B.inertiaSubgroup`) and $x$ over `eisensteinTorsionBar p 2 M` for some $M$, i.e. the elements of $J$ annihilated by the $M$-th power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal. Let $\varepsilon$ denote the ring homomorphism $\mathbb T \to$ `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` obtained from `heckeEvalForms p 2` (sending the variable at $\ell$ to $U_\ell$ or $T_\ell$ in weight $2$, level $p$) followed by `latticeRestrictHom p ∅`, the restriction of the Hecke action to the integral lattice in weight-two cusp forms. The assertion is that there exist $a, b \in \mathbb N$, an element $s_0 \in \Lambda$ and a family $t_m \in \mathbb T$ ($m \in \mathbb N$) such that, for all $m$: $\varepsilon(t_m)^2 - \varepsilon(t_m)$ and $\varepsilon(t_{m+1}) - \varepsilon(t_m)$ lie in the ideal generated by $2^m$; for every $s \in \Lambda$ there is $l \in \Lambda$ with $t_m \cdot s - s = 2^m l$; for every $t \in \mathbb T$ which maps $\Lambda$ into $2^{m+b}\Lambda$ (in the sense that each $t\cdot s$ with $s \in \Lambda$ equals $2^{m+b}l$ for some $l \in \Lambda$) the product $\varepsilon(t_m)\varepsilon(t)$ lies in the ideal generated by $2^m$; and for every $s \in \Lambda$ there is $t \in \mathbb T$ with $t\cdot s_0 \in \Lambda$ and $2^a s - t \cdot s_0 = 2^m l$ for some $l \in \Lambda$, the action on sequences being componentwise.
--
--   This packages, in the form needed later, the Eisenstein-ideal analysis of the $2$-adic Tate module of the inertia-displacement part of $J_0(p)$: an approximate idempotent tower cutting out the Eisenstein component together with an element $s_0$ generating $\Lambda$ up to a bounded power of $2$ and up to arbitrarily high $2$-adic precision, in the spirit of Mazur's rank-one freeness over the Eisenstein completion. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_family_tateModule_inf_pi_closure_inertia_smul_sub_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_quotient_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_addMonoidHom_family_tateModule_inf_pi_closure_inertia_smul_sub_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_natCard_ker_quotient_le), where the generator and the idempotents are turned into homomorphisms to Hecke-lattice quotients with controlled kernels.
